  "intro": "Third graders break words apart to read them. A prefix is added to the front of a word and changes its meaning (un- means not: unhappy = not happy). A suffix is added to the end (-ful means full of: helpful = full of help). Words can also be split into syllables. Knowing word parts helps you read and understand longer words.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "What does the prefix 'un-' mean in the word 'unlock'?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "A prefix changes the meaning of the base word.",
          "'Un-' means not or the opposite.",
          "So 'unlock' means to do the opposite of lock, to open."
        ],
        "answer": "Not / the opposite (to open)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "What does the suffix '-ful' mean in 'colorful'?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "A suffix is added to the end.",
          "'-ful' means full of.",
          "So 'colorful' means full of color."
        ],
        "answer": "Full of (full of color)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Break 'sunset' into two smaller words.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "A compound word is made of two words.",
          "'Sunset' = sun + set.",
          "So the two words are 'sun' and 'set.'"
        ],
        "answer": "Sun + set."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "What does 're-' mean in 'redo'?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "'Re-' means again."
        ],
        "answer": "Again (do again)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 5,
      "prompt": "What does '-less' mean in 'fearless'?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "'-less' means without."
        ],
        "answer": "Without (without fear)."
      }
    },
